 "notes": "Both SWP entries (Mem III p. 104 Khurbet Abu 'Adas, square centre 10.9 km; Mem III pp. 105-106 Khurbet 'Adaseh, 13.4 km) were found by similar name and are different places, not within 2 km; ignored. Many single-feature Kloner rows (burial caves, cisterns) treated as the feature's own row for dating. S3458 MB tomb is from the Comments field. S3422 rock-hewn ritual bath coded as pool, pool_def unclear (not said to be open). S3593 'pits' on a rock surface coded as pit. Columbarium caves coded as pit (not called burial). Rows with only rock-cuttings, winepresses, quarries or cupmarks not coded; E703 and E712 have no components."
